<p>Britain’s Labour Party has approved Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham’s request to enter the candidate selection process for the Makerfield by-election, the first step toward a possible return to Parliament and a potential challenge to Prime Minister Keir Starmer’s leadership. Burnham sought permission after Labour MP Josh Simons said Thursday that he would resign from the House of Commons, a move described as clearing a path for Burnham to seek the seat. Labour’s National Executive Committee said applications for the selection process opened Friday and close Monday, with the NEC due to endorse a candidate on Thursday; June 18 is described as the earliest likely date for the by-election. Reform UK, led by Nigel Farage, plans a major campaign for the seat after finishing second there in the 2024 general election, when Simons held Makerfield by 5,399 votes; Reform also won all eight local council wards in the constituency in recent local elections.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ARdJoJWlBiUkBdLjAaAKPtTRol5io9kAPGe8yIyDiNNPjFqFUlazZNYqurrP7RJT46vwX8bouvljh08Ub7XV4XJQdjCZnJsrythuErz4hb_RfD97peR6S1xSP_ttPpZK4SGu' alt='Mayor of Greater Manchester Andy Burnham was seen out running on Friday after announcing he would run to become an MP in the Makerfield by-election.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Leadership mechanics: Under Labour rules, a leadership contest would use preferential voting; a contender wins with more than 50% of first preferences, otherwise the last-placed candidate is eliminated and votes transfer.</li><li>Mayoral vacancy: If Burnham stands and wins, Greater Manchester would need a separate mayoral by-election because he still has two years left in his term.</li><li>Brexit stance: Burnham allies told supportive MPs he would not make rejoining the EU a central campaign message, despite previously telling a Labour Party conference he wanted Britain to rejoin in his lifetime.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Josh Simons: Simons said Parliament and the government had often become obstacles to getting things done and that the current government had not advanced the reforms his constituency needed; he called Burnham honest, trustworthy and principled. (<a href='https://www.stheadline.com/realtime-world/3572995/工黨議員辭職-為曼城市長競選黨魁鋪路'>St Headline</a>)</li><li>Nigel Farage and Reform UK: The i Paper reported that Reform planned to put Burnham’s pro-European record at the center of its campaign against him. (<a href='https://inews.co.uk/news/politics/farage-burnham-tactics-reform-crunch-by-election-4419656'>The i Paper</a>)</li><li>Wes Streeting: Streeting spoke to Burnham after resigning as health secretary in what one ally described as a ceasefire offer. An ally said Streeting offered to campaign for Burnham in Makerfield but still intended to contest any Labour leadership race. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/labour-tries-unite-stop-farage-wreck-leadership-fight-starmer-crisis-uk/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>Caroline Lucas: Former Green Party MP Caroline Lucas urged her party to help clear Burnham’s path to becoming prime minister. (<a href='https://www.thenational.scot/news/26111397.green-grandee-caroline-lucas-says-party-help-andy-burnham/'>The National</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/labour-tries-unite-stop-farage-wreck-leadership-fight-starmer-crisis-uk/'>Labour tries to unite — so Farage can’t wreck their leadership fight</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/uk-labour-party-says-it-will-let-burnham-run-for-parliamentary-seat'>UK Labour Party says it will let Burnham run for parliamentary seat</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/05/15/how-burnhams-by-election-will-transform-uk-politics/'>How Burnham’s By-Election Will Transform UK Politics</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/king-north-uk-governments-savior-seat-parliame